# User documentation (`docs/user-guide/`)

Hungarian end-user help shown in the CRM at **`/help`** (sidebar → **Súgó**). Markdown files with YAML frontmatter; permission-filtered TOC.

Complements:

- [`docs/inventory_and_logistics_flows.md`](../docs/inventory_and_logistics_flows.md) — technical flow map (agents/devs)
- [`docs/user-guide/`](../docs/user-guide/) — step-by-step user instructions

## When you MUST update user guide

Update the relevant `docs/user-guide/*.md` chapter(s) in the **same PR / task** when you change anything that alters **what users see or do**:

- New or renamed sidebar item or major route
- User-visible workflow (import wizard steps, movement confirm, logistics job states, HR request approval, product edit sections, etc.)
- UI button/menu label changes referenced in help steps
- New permission that gates a whole module or help section
- Phase milestone: new module shipped to users (add chapter + frontmatter `permissions`)

If you update [`docs/inventory_and_logistics_flows.md`](../docs/inventory_and_logistics_flows.md) per [`.cursor/rules/flows-documentation.mdc`](./flows-documentation.mdc), **also** check the matching user-guide chapter.

## How to update

1. Edit the affected markdown file(s) under `docs/user-guide/`.
2. Keep frontmatter: `title`, `description`, `order`, `section`, optional `permissions` (OR — user needs any listed key).
3. Use the chapter template: purpose → where in UI → required permission (plain language) → numbered steps with **exact UI labels** → tips → related `/help/...` links.
4. Set `*Utolsó frissítés: YYYY-MM*` at the bottom of each touched chapter.
5. Do **not** put Mongo field names, server action names, or Mermaid in user chapters.

## Section order

`Áttekintés` → `Készletkezelés` → `Logisztika` → `Könyvelés és HR` → `Titoktár` → `Adminisztráció`

New modules: add a `section` value and extend `groupHelpArticlesBySection` in [`apps/crm/src/lib/help/load-help.ts`](../apps/crm/src/lib/help/load-help.ts) if needed.

## Do not duplicate

User guide is **rewritten for operators**, not a copy of the flows doc. Link to routes (`/inventory`, …) and `/help/...` chapters; keep technical detail in flows doc + `docs/inventory.md` / `docs/hr.md`.
